A||||1||Derek85gT||How do I post pics in here?||||5||
Z||000000||Derek85gT||12-17-2001||11:32 AM||||I have a digital camera and would like to post a couple pics of me and my brothers cars.  I'm not sure if I should just copy and paste to this message or what...thx<P>p.s.  Brian just put the new hood on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||12-17-2001||11:37 AM||||It's really quite easy (if you have a PC- not a Mac).  First- download "PIP" (Pennock's Image Poster) from this link (or the one at the bottom of your screen):<BR><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/pip.html" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/pipbutton.gif">   </A><BR>There are instructions there as to how to download the software and set it up properly.  Once finished with the initial setup- it is really quite easy and intuitive: You simply select the pic you want to load using the browse button.  Then click the post button.  Finally, you paste the link (which is automatically pasted to the computer's clipboard when you upload the pic) into your message.  And you're done!  My only warning is to learn about file sizes- I usually don't post any images larger than 5 or 6 inches wide at screen resolution (72pixels per inch).  Anything beyond that can become unbearable to those with dialup connections.  <P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
